# Item rarity outline and UI widget shaders (client/MANIFEST.md "game_shaderfx" and "game_itemrarity", BASE.md 24). Items: a soft glow in the rarity colour around a dropped item of a rarity on the map and around items in inventory and container slots (UIItem decides: inventory slot styles and container "itemN" widgets; UIItem:setRarityOutlineMode(-1 auto, 0 never, 1 always)). Item::draw queues one DrawQueueItemItemOutline before the sprite and draws it from the sprite's final queue item at draw time: the sprite once more, grown by the reach, through a program that samples the sprite's alpha in rings and paints a smooth falloff where the sprite is transparent (the creature outline of 0038 does the same with a hard line). Colours, reach, the lowest rarity and pulsing come from Lua: Item.setRarityOutlineColor(rarity 1-15 or 16 = unique, r, g, b, a), Item.setRarityOutlineEnabled(onMap, inSlots), Item.setRarityOutlineStyle(width, minRarity, pulseFromRarity, pulseMs), item:getRarityOutlineColor(); with no colour set nothing is drawn. UI: the base parsed image-shader in OTUI but bound no Lua setter (corelib globals keeps setImageShader as a Lua field); UIWidget:setUiShader(name) / getUiShader() and setUiShaderParams(a, b, c, d) / getUiShaderParam(i) set the image shader and four values the shader reads as u_Params (PainterShaderProgram PARAMS_UNIFORM 17, set before each widget draw); an image shader that is not registered draws the plain image instead of nothing. Options (Graphics, new panel): rarityOutlineMap, rarityOutlineSlots, rarityFrameShine (on) and liquidOrbs (off). Touches item.h/.cpp, uiitem.h/.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp, framework drawqueue.h/.cpp, paintershaderprogram.h/.cpp, uiwidget.h, uiwidgetimage.cpp, luafunctions.cpp, client_settings dataset.lua and options/graphics.otui.
